;; top, a plain jump for every hero) the key pops out and lands on the pipe. Carried to the locked
;; door in the left wall (2, rows 11-12) it opens the door by itself; UP goes down into the crypt.
;; The townsperson, who lost the key, stands between. Once Simon is freed the door stands open
;; and the brick keeps its coins. Elsewhere the room is as it always was.
